Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Provenance of the example material
- All example audio was synthesized from scratch by make_test_sounds.py
  (sawtooth/square oscillators, sine partials, filtered noise). No samples,
  recordings, or third-party audio were used.
- The techniques (granular synthesis, cepstral envelope estimation,
  1-D optimal transport, cross-synthesis) are published signal-processing
  methods and are not owned by anyone.

Dependencies (not included here, keep their own licenses)
- numpy, scipy: BSD-3-Clause
- ffmpeg (optional, called as an external program): LGPL/GPL

Note on renders
Output made with DUDLEY belongs to whoever makes it, but it carries the
rights of whatever you feed in. Hybrids of your own recordings or of
public-domain/CC0 sources stay free. Hybrids of someone else's copyrighted
recording are derivatives of that recording. Every render's
.manifest.json records the SHA-1 of each input, so the provenance of any
piece can be traced.
